# Reference — TA: Kingdoms Unit IDs

Every unit definition shipped in *Total Annihilation: Kingdoms* (base
game + *Iron Plague* expansion), extracted directly from the
flattened install's `units/*.fbi`. Counts as of the GoG release:
**{{.TotalUnits}} units total** across {{len .Sides}} side(s).

Each row's `Code` is the unit's `unitname=` (uppercased — the lookup
key the rest of the game's data refers to). TA:K uses 3-letter side
prefixes: ARA = Aramon, TAR = Taros, VER = Veruna, ZON = Zhon,
CRE = Creon (Iron Plague), plus MON/LIF/NPC for monsters, wildlife,
and campaign NPCs.

Cost is in **mogrium** (TA:K's single combined resource). Weapons
are listed by their inline `[WEAPONn]` `name=` field, comma-separated.
Each row's portrait is the 64×48 JPG from `anims/buildpic/<unitname>.jpg`
in the install, copied verbatim into [`img/tak-units/`](img/tak-units/).

See the kbot docs:
- [FBI field dictionary](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/tdf.md#appendix-a--fbi-field-dictionary)
  (TA-focused but the parser is shared)
- [TA: Kingdoms research notes](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/takmap.md)

